# Anti-Slop Design: Frontend & UI Rules

When editing or creating user interfaces:
- Never generate generic "AI Dark Mode" purple/indigo radial gradients.
- Never use raw emojis as UI icons; use Lucide/Phosphor SVGs.
- Enforce the 1-to-3 UX rule (1 primary action, max 3 secondary).
- Global filters/date-pickers belong in the page header, never inside individual cards.
- Support 8 interactive states on all interactive controls.
- Snappy transitions (<200ms) with `cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1)`.
- Grade output against the 7-Axis Quality Gate in `SKILL.md`.
